{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118077-dark-eras-crusades-thread","id":1118077,"title":"[Dark Eras] Crusades Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-18T22:28:37-07:00","id":1118077,"title":"[Dark Eras] Crusades Thread","content":"Watching great sum-up of Crusades period, I returning to my idea from almost 15 years now to run game about this Era. Video is here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SpVEkH14Jrc\" data-code=\"SpVEkH14Jrc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/SpVEkH14Jrc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Now, Crusaders killed <i>many</i> people. In <b>CoD</b> 2E rules, Integrity still makes killing other human Breaking Point. <b>So how our God-smiting knights would go on Crusade, fight there for few years, and return to homeland somehow sane? </b>They would kill hundreds of people, each one of knights returning from Holy Land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T22:44:25-07:00","id":1118080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118077-dark-eras-crusades-thread#post1118077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watching great sum-up of Crusades period, I returning to my idea from almost 15 years now to run game about this Era. Video is here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SpVEkH14Jrc\" data-code=\"SpVEkH14Jrc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/SpVEkH14Jrc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Now, Crusaders killed <i>many</i> people. In <b>CoD</b> 2E rules, Integrity still makes killing other human Breaking Point. <b>So how our God-smiting knights would go on Crusade, fight there for few years, and return to homeland somehow sane? </b>They would kill hundreds of people, each one of knights returning from Holy Land.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not likely an answer you'll like, but the easiest answer is that it's a game, not a scientific simulations. There will be place the game system breaks down and that's fine. CofD is very much not a mass combat wargame, so it makes perfect sense that Intgrety is going to need some adjustment if you want a realistic portrayal of the Crusades.<br /> <br /> Now, all that said, there are possibilities. I was listening to Dan Carlin's Punic Nightmares today where he talks about the differences between moder War and ancient war. Modern war is a constant assault on your senses where something terrible could happen at any moment. Ancient war kept you safe most days, but on the one day you did have to fight, you have to basically act like a serial killer or you die. Mechanically, where would that leave us? I'd say that each person you kill individually does not provoke an Integrity check in ancient war. Instead, the entire battle is one integrity check that is likely to be heavily, heavily penalized due to the number of people you may have to kill. You're also looking multiple persistent conditions being levied... but an Integraty drop of one, maybe two at the most. <br /> <br /> The Integraty Through Attrition system from Hurt Locker could be another possibility. <br /> <br /> Don't forget that raising Integrity is also a possibility, and that most warriors would do something to help their resolve and deal with the PTSD. that could be enough to at least slow the loss of Integrity over rated by repurchasing some of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T22:55:29-07:00","id":1118085,"title":"","content":"Believing you're doing what's right and/or what needs to be done is what helps people get through these things. In Chronicles, this is represented by various bonuses to one's Breaking Point roll, with the added benefit that closeness with one's comrades and things like absolution from religious officials would help stabilize or even rebuild one's Integrity.<br /> <br /> It also helps that there weren't supernatural creatures running around scaring the Integrity out of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T23:08:17-07:00","id":1118088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118077-dark-eras-crusades-thread?p=1118085#post1118085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Believing you're doing what's right and/or what needs to be done is what helps people get through these things. In Chronicles, this is represented by various bonuses to one's Breaking Point roll, with the added benefit that closeness with one's comrades and things like absolution from religious officials would help stabilize or even rebuild one's Integrity.<br /> <br /> It also helps that there weren't supernatural creatures running around scaring the Integrity out of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also worth pointing out that kill or be killed could come into play here under the umbrella of &quot;doing what one must.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T00:09:10-07:00","id":1118098,"title":"","content":"I thought about using only one Breaking Point roll per battle and giving bonuses. For Crusaders, I was thinking that beside normal war time bonuses - your army morale, commanders charisma and 'For King and Country' - they probably would have also bonus to fight 'enemies of Christianity'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T00:26:28-07:00","id":1118102,"title":"","content":"Outside of unusual circumstances, I would only have one breaking point per scene because it is easy enough to do several things in a scene that could be a breaking point. Battles were short so that would be a scene. Well, the actual combat in battles was short. Everyone typically had time to prepare so there is meditation for a bonus on the roll. Final point, professional soldiers were rare. Typical fighters would participate in a few battles and retire to go back to their job. Okay one more, for those that essentially were professional soldiers, many of them would not be described as sane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}